# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Plan 00201 Tasks 2.10 (UX fixes) and 2.11 (security fixes): deploys the ccy launcher
# 3.98.10, which requires container 2.65, so the next ccy launch rebuilds the image once. In a
# team session a human's accents, other scripts and emoji read as written in the delivery
# block; the agent's answer is an Element reply to the message (`say --re`), and Element shows
# the agent's avatar under each human message it received; the skill and delivery frame carry
# the security rules (plugin 1.2.2). Rebuilds ccy-teams: Enter on a team row has "Open every
# team in Element, a window each"; a run that used sudo drops the credential before it exits,
# Ctrl-C included; the launch block names who can direct a session; a copied password serves
# one paste. cc --teams gets the new deny rules and consent text. Every team session must then
# be relaunched: a session on an older image silently drops a reply from a new one, refusing it
# as an edit.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plans 00161/00201 security fixes (homeserver and infrastructure): play-agent-bus first takes a
# fresh backup of every running team (failing the run if one fails, so the worst case is a known
# `agent-bus-install restore`), then installs Tuwunel 1.9.4 (from 1.9.3) and a re-sandboxed
# homeserver unit, so it RESTARTS EVERY TEAM'S HOMESERVER (a few seconds each; members reconnect
# by themselves). Each homeserver then sees only its own team's directory and no sibling
# process; allows three wrong passwords, then one per five minutes, per account; refuses
# display-name changes; caps a request at 10 MB. Bootstrap deletes the stored admin password
# (the token stays) and empties any agent_bus.status event under a key that is not a user ID.
# The applied stamps become 0640 in a 0750 directory, group the desktop user's primary group.
# Plan 00201 Tasks 2.10 and 2.11: agent-bus-install software puts the same pingbus and kit in
# /usr/local/share/agent-bus/kit, so `cc --teams` sessions and LXC members get the same
# replies, read receipts, readable text and security rules, and must be restarted too (an old
# one drops replies as edits); and the agent-bus seat commands ccy and cc launch through, so a
# launch naming a stopped team says `ccy-teams apply <team>`, an unknown one lists the teams
# here, and `seat take` and `seat remove` end with `sudo -k`. No firewall rule changes; a team
# that still reads "out of date: software" afterwards is applied from ccy-teams. The owner's
# checks: Plan 00201 ACCEPTANCE-owner.md, from its "Morning start".
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
# Plan 00161: its triage, deploy and acceptance again. Triage now reads the bus address from
# agent_bus_address in host_vars, as deploy and acceptance do, so H1 and H2 test agentbus0; the
# deploy's throwaway team zz-deploy-check now names GitHub's API as forge_api, the only one
# agent-bus-install accepts (it is installed, checked and removed, nothing is contacted); the
# acceptance's M2 leg reads the delivery envelope's first line and accepts an answer by
# `pingbus send` as well as `pingbus recv`.
00161-agent-team-bus-matrix
# Plan 00201: the automated two-team acceptance again on the new pingbus, kit and homeservers.
00201-ccy-teams-many-teams-per-session-descriptions-and-a-picker
# Plan 00201 final review fixes: deploys the ccy launcher 3.98.11, which requires container
# 2.66, so the next ccy launch rebuilds the image once. Element shows an agent's avatar under a
# human's message only once the delivery is in the agent's conversation; the skill and delivery
# frame say to JSON-decode the history text before comparing (plugin 1.2.3). Rebuilds
# ccy-teams: while the Clipboard Indicator extension is on, a new password is not offered to
# the clipboard (the extension would use up the paste and keep the password); it says why.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00201 final review fixes: the pre-swap backup also runs when this checkout renders a
# running team's tuwunel.toml differently (a homeserver restart), not only for a new Tuwunel or
# unit; agent-bus-install software puts the new pingbus in the kit for `cc --teams` sessions and
# LXC members. No firewall rule changes.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
